2026-10-13T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Bao holds a bounded set
 # uuid: 60fba0cd-3b7a-59da-8af7-48c78bd8ffbf
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l2
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-10-13T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Bao's storage stays the same size whatever the number of users, sessions or requests
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2316) 'weftspun-bao on weftspun-fdb, every secrets engine and auth method mounted on it, and the plugins built for it
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Bao stays the same size however many users, sessions or requests arrive.
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Bao's default is to keep a lease for every dynamic secret, so an engine on the defaults grows with its traffic until a write fails.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Read RFD66606-2317 next, the first engine held to this rule.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Bao holds a bounded set
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2316) '- Bao stores keys, configuration, policies and ReBAC tuples, and nothing that grows with users, sessions or requests (operator, 2026-10-13).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2316) '- An engine that issues a credential per request keeps no lease and no record of it. The credential carries its own expiry and is never revoked.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2316) '- Application data lives outside Bao, in the service that owns it.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2316) '- Every engine ships a growth gate: issuing many credentials leaves the engine's storage unchanged, and a control that stores each one fails it.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2316) '- RFD66606-2140, Bao on FDB.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2316) '- RFD66606-2353, Bao runs three replicas on the FDB machines.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2316) '- RFD66606-2200, ReBAC agent roles.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2316) '- RFD66606-2317, the first engine held to this rule.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Why the limit is part of the design
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2316) 'FoundationDB refuses a value over 100,000 bytes and a transaction over 10,000,000 bytes, so the limit is part of the design and not a setting.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Sources
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Written on 2026-10-13 from the operator's note that Bao has a hard data limit by design. The FDB backend was read in our OpenBao fork: `Put` calls one `Set` with the whole encrypted entry and splits nothing. The value and transaction limits are FoundationDB's published known limits. Neither limit has been measured on our cluster yet; the first engine's end-to-end test writes an entry just under and just over 100,000 bytes and records which one FDB refuses.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2316) 'What may be stored
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2316) 'An entry belongs in Bao when the count of such entries is set by the operator, not by traffic:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2316) '- signing keys, CA keys and certificates of issuers;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2316) '- engine and mount configuration;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2316) '- policies, cert roles and ReBAC tuples;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2316) '- one-off secrets an operator puts there, such as an API token.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2316) 'These do not belong in Bao:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2316) '- a lease or record per issued credential;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2316) '- sessions, messages, counters, logs or audit trails of a service;
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2316) '- files and blobs of any size.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2316) 'An engine that needs to hold a resource for a while, such as a slot in a shared cap, may still use a lease, because the number of leases is capped by the resource and not by traffic. Its growth gate then checks that the lease count stays at or under the cap.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2316) 'The growth gate
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Each engine's unit tests run against `logical.InmemStorage` and count its keys with a recursive `List` before and after issuing 1,000 credentials. The gate passes when the count and the summed value size are unchanged. The control flips the engine to store each credential and must fail the same gate. The end-to-end test does the same against a dev server and also checks that the response carries no lease id.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2316) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-10-13T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2316) 'Bao's storage is FoundationDB on three small machines, and the FDB backend writes each entry as one FDB value.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2316  1 LINE
 Text:Written
